[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2473664406","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99102#issuecomment-2473664406","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99102","id":2473664406,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6TcR-W","user":{"login":"Lazy-Rabbit-2001","id":22123964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTIzOTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22123964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","html_url":"https://github.com/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-13T13:44:53Z","updated_at":"2024-11-13T13:44:53Z","body":"Kinda off-topic, but it surprised me that the back braces will not get overlapped. In previous versions, trying completing your code inside a couple of round brackets will remove the back brace if the completion is about a method or a keyword with `()`, like this:\r\n```GDScript\r\nprint(is_inside_tree() # <- Here the back brace of `is_inside_tree()` is missing, or overlapping with the outer one.\r\n```\r\nI'm not sure if it is this pr or some other pr in this version that fixed this bug, or maybe it's because I haven't tested edge situation yet. But it seems to be a good sign.","autho